A||N||9||Monkeyman||Need help adding power accessories!!!||||9||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||06-23-2001||06:47 PM||||I'm in the middle of adding p/mirrors and locks to 4Play.  It's not going bad, but I'm kinda stuck on a few things.  I'd like to finish the job tomorrow.<P>1)  I can't seem to get the lock actuators to work.  I have the passenger door completely wired up including the lock relay, but the actuators won't move.  I can hear the relay click, but that's it.  I've hooked up both actuators, but that didn't help.  Do both actuators need to be grounded to the doors (through the mounting bolts) for either of them to work?  HELP!!!!<P>2)  Where the heck does the p/mirror harness plug into for the power?  It looks like it's supposed to plug into the power distribution  box (why not?  everything else does), but I can't seem to find a way to make the plug fit.  <P>3)  Does it matter where things are plugged into the power distribution box?  Can they be plugged in anywhere they fit?<P>All I have left to do is the drivers door, run my stereo wiring, and put everything back together (dash, center console, etc).  I'd really like to get this finished tomorrow so I can drive to work Monkday (umm...I mean 'Monday'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>Any help would be greatly appreciated.  As a matter of fact, if anyone has time for a phone call and can help for sure, email me with your phone # and I'll call you this evening (I'll be on line off and on most of the evening).<P>MM||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||06-23-2001||09:11 PM||||The lock selonoids are not grounded to the body they work by reversing polarity to the unit, same thing for the mirrors. You can test the lock units by running the 2 wires from the selonoids directly to a power source and you should hear them clunk, then reverse the wires and they should clunk again. <BR>Are you using the Ford switch for the mirrors? You can use any hot wire as a power source for the mirrors( I tap into the radio lead usually).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||06-23-2001||10:39 PM||||Sounds like you've been sort of busy there.<BR>Ring||||reg||14
Z||000003||FieroJoe||06-23-2001||11:58 PM||||When I added my power locks they would work erratically, just turned out to be poor connections.  Clean off any corrosion on the solenoid's connector and the wiring harness connector, that is after you make sure they work fine by using Phil's advice.<P>As for the power distribution box, I think this should help...out of a 87 Helm manual<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/whiteboxpinout_2.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-24-2001||01:17 AM||||Thanx, guys.<P>Phil--I don't have a good power source.  I bought the wiring harnesses, switches and actuators off of 007Doug, so I'm assuming that everything works and is in good condition.  I'm sure he tested it before he removed it from the donor car.  I'm not using the Ford switch right now.  I'm not very good with anything mechanical/electrical.  I just want to get everything working, then I'll decided if I want to go that route.  If I do, I'll let you know how things went.<P>Keith--I'll give you a buzz 1st thing in the am.  Probably around 10, give or take a couple hours.  All depends how successful I am with everyones' suggestions.  Thanx.<P>Joe--That's the second power distribution box pic I've received tonight.  Each is slightly different, but between the two I should be able to get it figured out.  The connections are clean (I sprayed everything with WD40) so I don't think that's the problem.  If I can't make it work, I'll just call Indiana resto guy for help.  He was going to do the labor for me anyway, but I was in a hurry (read::impatient) to get it done.  <P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-24-2001||03:05 AM||||Ford switch? You mean the round knob thing that fits the factory hole? I have a fiero mirror switch you you need it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||06-24-2001||03:13 AM||||Ford p/mirror switch.  Joystick style.  Fits beautifully in the stock manual mirror housing.  I found mine in a late '80s/early '90s Escort.  Phil Randolph did his mirrors this way and he's currently converting his wifes car the same way.  I may end up doing this (just to be different), but I got a stock switch with the wiring harness so I'll use that for now.  Once I get everything hooked up and working well, I may decide to undertake the wiring challenge, but I'm a little nervous doing it now.  Thanx for the offer.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||06-24-2001||09:58 PM||||The job's finished!!  I just have to wait for my door panels to get reupholstered and I'm done.  I have a couple of problems, though.  1st, the passenger side mirror only works left/right not up/down.  I rechecked all the connections and they're good (no corrosion--sprayed with WD40).  I guess I need a new motor assy.  The other problem is really wierd.  My p/locks work, but the switches seem to be backwards.  When I press the 'Unlock' button, the doors lock (and vice versa).  What the heck's up with this????  I gotta figure this one out before I install a RKE system (in a couple of weeks).  Any suggestions??<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||06-24-2001||10:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>The other problem is really wierd.  My p/locks work, but the switches seem to be backwards.  When I press the 'Unlock' button, the doors lock (and vice versa).  What the heck's up with this???? <BR>MM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oooopsy!  I dont think you can mix up the connections on the relay, so I bet the switches are installed backwards in the door handle plates.  I dont think you can plug in the connector from the door harness to the switch backwards either.  There are different switches for driver and pass. doors.  The Lock button should be towards the back of the car on each side.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||06-25-2001||06:51 AM||||Thanx.  I'll check after work this afternoon.  The switches/housings came out of the donor car together and I think they were factory but who knows.  What else could be wrong?<P>MM||||reg||1
